GO term ID: 0018505  
Name: cis-1,2-dihydro-1,2-dihydroxynaphthalene dehydrogenase activity  
Definition: Catalysis of the reaction: cis-1,2-dihydronaphthalene-1,2-diol + NAD+ = naphthalene-1,2-diol + NADH + H+.  

The primary reaction described in the definition is the catalytic transfer of a hydrogen atom from cis-1,2-dihydronaphthalene-1,2-diol to NAD+, resulting in the formation of naphthalene-1,2-diol and the reduction of NAD+ to NADH. This reaction is central to the function of the enzyme described by the GO term.  

